\par\par \b \uc2 Chinese Yuan Swings Versus Dollar, With Possible  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kenan Machado \par \uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2018\par 12:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The yuan touched on Thursday its strongest level against the U.S. dollar since a surprise devaluation in August 2015, before reversing some in late Asian trading hours as the dollar rebounded broadly.\par \par \uc2 The gyrations came as the greenback continued its slide against a variety of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  early on Thursday. The latest drop came after U.S. Treasury Secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  said overnight that "a weaker dollar is good for trade."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ICE\uc2  Dollar Index, which measures the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of six others, fell as much as 0.5% to hit three-year lows.\par \par \uc2 But it started a broad rebound in midafternoon Asian trading and was recently down 0.2%. Against the yuan, the greenback then moved from as low as 6.3148 yuan to 6.3375 yuan in roughly 30 minutes, according to data from Wind Info.\par \par \uc2 The yuan was recently at 6.3215 per dollar, equivalent to a 1% drop for the greenback versus late-afternoon levels Wednesday, with onshore trading to end at 11:3\par \par \uc2 0 p.m. China time.\par \par \uc2 The initial rebound in dollar-yuan was likely driven by state-run Chinese banks' buying the greenback on the instructions of \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Stephen Innes, head of Asian trading at \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  broker Oanda. He noted that sell orders against the dollar versus the yuan steadily entered the inter-bank trading system Thursday morning, after the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  set the daily trading midpoint for the yuan versus the dollar at a two-year high.\par \par \uc2 However, there were a number of offers to buy the dollar at 2:40 p.m. Hong Kong time, sending it jumping versus the yuan.\par \par \uc2 Computer-driven trading likely amplified moves amid pre-programmed stop-losses at hedge funds, said a head of trading at a foreign bank in Hong Kong and Mr. Innes. "These funds likely thought, 'I have had enough of this,'" Mr. Innes added.\par \par \uc2 China has been trying to give the impression that it is liberalizing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. As such, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely limit market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Iris Pang, an economist for Greater \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Dutch bank ING.\par \par \uc2 But it appears to her that a dollar around 6.30 yuan is as strong as officials are willing to tolerate at the moment. "But if that level is relevant tomorrow or next week, no one knows," Ms. Pang said.\par \par \uc2 While some investors continue to expect the yuan to rise against the dollar over time, they say they have started to hold on to their bullish bets for shorter periods, given the dollar's roughly 4.5% drop versus the yuan since mid-December.\par \par \uc2 "We are fairly comfortable holding a long renminbi position in our portfolios, but it's generally a result of our bond allocation to China, " said Edmund Goh, Asian fixed-income investment manager at Aberdeen Asset Management in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 -Saumya Vaishampayan contributed to this article. \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 25, 2018 06:18 ET (11:18 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180125ee1p00154\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
