\par\par \b \uc2 China Unlikely to Focus on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Reform This Year -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2018\par 11:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1056 GMT - \b \highlight22\uc2 China central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market via the counter-cyclical factor has eased significantly since 4Q of 2017, says \uc2 OCBC\uc2  economist \uc2 Tommy Xie\uc2 . The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  's latest tweak to its daily fixing mechanism may mark a nascent step for the yuan to return to the path towards a free floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but Beijing is unlikely to aggressively pursue \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform this year as it focuses on deleveraging, he says. "Should the U.S. dollar unexpectedly strengthen in the global market in 2018, we think the CCF may be back to the centre stage."(liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1053 GMT - Carmignac maintains its short position on \uc2 German government\uc2  bonds, says \uc2 Didier Saint-Georges\uc2 , managing director at the asset management company. The rationale behind this positioning is that Carmignac considers 2018 likely to be a more trying year for the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  than 2017 as the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  carries on with its normalization plans. The 10-year German bund yield is trading at 0.45%, up from levels around 0.30% in mid-December. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 1034 GMT - The Hellenic Confederation of Commerce and Enterprises says it expects Greece's retail commerce to post its first positive turnover in eight years in 2017. During the first nine months of 2017 all indices turned higher, a trend expected to have extended to the last quarter of 2017, it says in a report. The turnover index rose by 2.3%. From 2009 to 2016 turnover recorded a contraction of 29.1%. (nektaria.stamouli@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1033 GMT - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could break the link between quantitative easing and the inflation outlook at its March meeting, Dominick DeAlto, \uc2 BNP Paribas Asset Management\uc2  's fixed-income CIO, says in a note. Many market participants currently see the inflation outlook as a factor guiding the \uc2 ECB\uc2  's decisions regarding the size and length of its asset-purchase program. Delinking the two could be a prelude to the end of net asset purchases later this year. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 1033 GMT - Analysts generally don't see the upcoming Italian election as a risk event, but even if it does boost volatility in the stock market, the reaction in corporate bonds could be low. Data compiled by \uc2 Amundi\uc2  show that the correlation between euro-credit spreads and equity-implied volatility has declined since the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's corporate sector purchase program was announced. The Brexit referendum was the first real test to this new regime and subsequent risk events, such as the Italian constitutional referendum in late 2016 and the French presidential elections, confirmed the reduced correlation. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 1026 GMT - Another data release, another positive surprise for the eurozone as industrial production came in stronger than expected in November. \uc2 Eurostat\uc2  's figures showed output was up 1% on the month and 3.2% on the year, compared to a consensus forecast of 0.6% on the month and 2.9% on the year. \uc2 Eurostat\uc2  also raised its estimates for October. The encouraging part of the breakdown for the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that capital goods led the rise, fresh evidence that a pickup in investment spending is finally underway. The discouraging part was that the rise was largely down to a jump in Germany, but there is a lot of month-to-month volatility in these figures and there are other indications that the pickup is broader based.(paul.hannon@wsj.com Twitter: @PaulHannon29)\par \par \uc2 1014 GMT - Junk-rated \uc2 Com Hem\uc2  's credit will clearly benefit from the merger with \uc2 Tele2\uc2  , as the combined entity should have an "investment grade commensurate" credit profile, \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  analysts say in a note. But investors thinking of buying the Swedish telecom 's debt on the back of this may be disappointed, as Swedish krona-denominated \uc2 Com Hem\uc2  bonds have already rallied on the back of the merger news. Therefore, the analysts don't see much upside potential left and downgrade \uc2 Com Hem\uc2  bonds to marketweight from overweight. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 1013 GMT - \uc2 Gecina\uc2  's asset sales worth around EUR570 million are positive from a credit perspective, but the French real estate firm must reduce leverage to avoid a downgrade at \uc2 Moody's\uc2  . The rating company expects \uc2 Gecina\uc2  to use proceeds from the sale to repay outstanding short-term debt. Assuming all of the proceeds go for short-term debt repayment, the gross debt-to-total assets ration should decline to 42.2% from 44% at mid-2017. But if \uc2 Gecina\uc2  fails to reduce this ratio to under 40% by the end of 2018, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  would consider downgrading it from A3. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0958 GMT - The \uc2 U.K. Debt Management Office\uc2  's auction of the 1.75% 2037 gilt Thursday should feature a higher cover ratio than the issue's previous reopening in October, not least due to the lower amount offered, according to \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  . The DMO is offering GBP2.25 billion Thursday, down from GBP2.5 billion in October. Back then, the cover ratio-which reflects bids received versus the amount offered-stood at 1.85 times. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0949 GMT - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric in the minutes to December's meeting, due at 1230 GMT, should be "fairly neutral" says ING. Policymakers are "likely to be wary" that a stronger euro could dampen the eurozone's economic recovery. ING estimates the \uc2 ECB\uc2  's "pain threshold"--the point where \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation hurts the economy--is "a sharp move above 1.25," and says policymakers will be wary of this. "We expect to see fairly neutral \uc2 ECB\uc2  rhetoric, at least until they are comfortable to allow markets to price in the next stages of policy normalisation." It expects EUR/USD to stabilize around 1.20. EUR/USD last trades flat at 1.1946.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0937 GMT - The dollar rises on Thursday, with the DXY index up 0.2% at 92.46, reversing some of the previous day's losses after Chinese authorities denied Wednesday's media reports that China may be cutting or slowing down purchases of U.S. Treasuries. But "any correction higher in DXY likely to be limited to 93.00," ING says, since "the dollar is losing its status as an investment \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." EUR/USD trades down 0.1^ at 1.1939. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT - The Canadian dollar falls versus the U.S. dollar, with USD/CAD up 0.3% at 1.2589, on reports Canada believes U.S. President Trump will announce the U.S. is pulling out of \uc2 NAFTA\uc2  . \uc2 RBC\uc2  says this has caused markets to trim expectations of a rate increase next week, with the implied probability falling to 73% from 88%, although it doesn't think this will be enough to "derail a hike." The Bank of Canada increased rates twice last year and another three increases are expected in 2018. So far, rate rises of more than 80 basis points for 2018 are priced into the Canadian dollar, \uc2 RBC\uc2  says.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 11, 2018 05:56 ET (10:56 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180111ee1b000y8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
