\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-China yuan to slip as US dollar regains lost ground\b0\par\par\uc2 618 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2017\par 06:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=CNY= CNY poll data\par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=inr= INR poll data\par \par \uc2 By Vivek Mishra\par \par \uc2 BENGALURU, Nov 9 (Reuters) - China's yuan is expected to weaken slightly over the coming year as renewed hopes of sweeping tax reform in the United States and gradual \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  rate hikes hand back control to the dollar, a Reuters poll of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists showed.\par \par \uc2 Having fallen since early January, the dollar index, which measures the greenback against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has rebounded nearly 3 percent after the Fed announced plans in September for its balance sheet reduction.\par \par \uc2 That has driven expectations for the yuan to surrender some of 2017's gains, according to the latest poll of over 60 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts taken Nov 6-8.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has gained over 4 percent this year, is now forecast to fall more than 1 percent to 6.72 per dollar in a year from Wednesday's level of around 6.63. That is similar to predictions made last month.\par \par \uc2 But those expectations are largely dependent on a strong dollar, which is not at all certain. Any support for the greenback hinges mainly on Congress passing major tax reform, the Reuters poll of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  found.\par \par \uc2 "The yuan experienced a rapid appreciation in September, but it is not what the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  (\uc2 PBoC\uc2 ) wishes to see," said Li Yishuang, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 China Securities\uc2  in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 "So, I think two-way movements of the exchange rate will become more obvious in the next year, and it will depend in great part on the movement of the U.S. dollar index."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision in September to remove a reserve requirement on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on financial institutions is also slowing the pace of yuan appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the PBoC allowed the yuan to fall by on Sept. 11 setting a 2 percent lower mid-point reference rate of 6.4997 and on Wednesday lowered it again to 6.6277 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The PBoC will keep managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the daily USD/CNY fix, using the counter-cyclical factor to guide the market if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deviates from fundamentals," noted Irene Cheung, senior strategist for Asia at ANZ.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to stay away from official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to be one of the fastest-growing major global economies in a separate Reuters poll, the latest predictions pointed to slower growth next year compared to 2017. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2e7JFpt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2e7JFpt}}}\par \par \uc2 That could play an important role in yuan movements over the coming year.\par \par \uc2 "We expect CNY to slightly depreciate again over the coming quarters against the U.S. dollar, due to weaker growth prospects for the Chinese economy," wrote Hao Zhou, EM strategist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 , in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 India's rupee, which has gained over 4 percent this year, is expected to trade in a tight range against the dollar over the coming 12 months.\par \par \uc2 Median forecasts showed the rupee trading at 65.15 per dollar in a year, not far from the 64.98 it was at on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "We see a tug of war between the U.S. dollar and the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's compulsion to recoup \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in the coming year," said Indranil Sengupta, India chief economist at Bank of America Merrill Lynch.\par \par \uc2 (For other stories from the global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll:) (Polling by Shaloo Shrivastava and Khushboo Mittal; Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-11-9T06:00:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020171109edb9006k6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
