\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2017\par 01:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Financial Stocks Push U.S. Indexes Higher \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rising financial shares pushed U.S. stock indexes higher. All three major U.S. stock indexes notched fresh records. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Oil Rises on Concern Over Global Political Tensions \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices rose as tensions in the Middle East and concerns about U.S. policy in the region added to gains at the end of last week. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China's Xi Approaches a New Term With a Souring Taste for Markets \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As a Communist Party congress opens, the pro-market talk from President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xi Jinping\f28 \uc2 \f2  's first term has faded as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's priorities turn to economic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and supporting state companies. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Trump to Meet With Yellen to Discuss Fed Chief Renomination \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to meet Thursday with Federal Reserve Chairwoman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  to discuss the possibility of nominating her for a second term as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief, according to a person familiar with the matter. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Economic Crackdown on North Korea Begins, Belatedly \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 North Korea has long evaded international sanctions to keep its nuclear and missile programs moving ahead, but that may finally be drawing to a close, Gerald F. Seib writes. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CFPB Enforcement Chief to Step Down \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau\f28 \uc2 \f2  's enforcement chief, Anthony Alexis, plans to leave the agency, a move that could herald a significant change in the way the regulator polices financial companies. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Beijing Blas\u233\'00\'E9 as Government Bond Yields Keep Climbing \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing's apparent lack of concern over the recent bond selloff-prices Monday hit their lowest since 2014-contrasts with heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in stock and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets ahead of this week's big party conclave. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Cutting Corporate Taxes Would Boost Workers' Income, White House Says \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cutting the U.S. corporate tax rate would boost average household income by $4,000 a year, the White House said, contradicting many economists who say shareholders and not workers would see most of the benefit from such a reduction. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Why Can't We Have a Decent Stock Bubble? \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After an eight-year bull market and the cheapest borrowing costs in history, the big surprise is that the stock market isn't higher. The simple answer is that the public is wary after the dot-com bubble of 2000 and the housing bubble of 2007. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Euro-Area Exports Leap Despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Gain \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exports of goods from the eurozone jumped in August, suggesting the euro's appreciation against other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has yet to crimp economic growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 16, 2017 19:00 ET (23:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020171016edag003c4\par 