\par\par \b \uc2 Time May be Here for Yuan Shorts -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,484 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2017\par 05:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0329 GMT - After rising nearly 6% versus the Korean won in a near-uninterrupted run higher the past 2 months, RBC says now's the time to short the offshore yuan against the won. That as moves the past week suggest \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is reining in yuan appreciation by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market, setting the dollar-yuan fix higher than moves in major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  imply and accumulating value-adjusted \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the investment bank adds. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0230 GMT - China has now fixed the yuan stronger against the dollar for 11 straight sessions -- the longest such streak since authorities ended the yuan's hard peg against the dollar in 2005. Monday's reference rate for the dollar against the yuan was 6.4997, which set the yuan weaker than where it ended against the dollar in onshore trading Friday. In recent action, the yuan fell 0.6% against the greenback; one dollar bought 6.4981 yuan, compared with CNY6.4617 at the close of trading Friday. (saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com; @saumvaish)\par \par \uc2 0220 GMT - China's move to remove the reserve requirement for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards will save trading costs and make the yuan more flexible and market-driven, says CICC. But it also says that the move is unlikely to reverse market sentiment for the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose rate will be determined by domestic economy. CICC says Beijing could consider phasing out its capital control measures in response to the recent surge of the yuan. It may start with loosening control over residents' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, CICC says. (grace.zhu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0211 GMT - The first rung on the Australian property ladder is a big step, and fewer people have made the transition from renter to buyer since the global financial crisis, a paper released by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  says. But it also notes those who do get on the ladder are more financially stable than past cohorts. So while "generation rent" is an important trend for the country, the paper says the additional money needed for a deposit is also a sign of financial discipline that's associated with fewer subsequent difficulties. (robb.stewart@wsj.com; @RobbMStewart)\par \par \uc2 0158 GMT - EUR/GBP Intraday: Watch 0.9090. The pair is clearly in a down trend, and remains under pressure below its nearest resistance at 0.9145. Both the 20-period and 50-period moving averages are heading downward, and should call for further downsides. In addition, the relative strength index broke down a rising trend line, and is now below its neutrality area at 50. Therefore, as long as the resistance at 0.9145 is not surpassed, the risk of the break below 0.9090 remains high. Alternative scenario, above 0.9145, look for further upside with 0.9170 & 0.9200 as targets. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized 0investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9] (analysts@tradingcentral.com)\par \par \uc2 0157 GMT - EUR/JPY Intraday: Turning up. The pair bounced off its key support at 129.45, which should limit any downside room. The relative strength index is turning up, and broke above its neutrality area at 50. Besides, the 20-period moving average is now below the prices, and plays a support role. To sum up, as long as 129.75 holds on the downside, look for a new bounce to 130.40 & 130.65 in extension. Alternatively, below 129.75, expect a new pullback to 129.45 & 129.10 as targets. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized 0investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9] (analysts@tradingcentral.com)\par \par \uc2 0157 GMT - USD/CAD Intraday: Upside prevails. The pair remains bullish above 1.2115, and is likely to post a new rebound. The 20-period moving average has turned up, and has also crossed above the 50-period one (a bullish signal). In addition, the relative strength index is heading upward, calling for a new rise. In which case, as long as 1.2115 is not broken, likely advance to 1.2175 & 1.2205 in extension. Alternatively, below 1.2115, expect a return to 1.2060 & 1.2000 as targets. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized 0investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9] (analysts@tradingcentral.com)\par \par \uc2 0130 GMT - Japan's machinery orders for July indicate corporate capital spending remains broadly sluggish despite bright spots in areas like autos and transportation. Machinery orders excluding the ship and power sectors rose 8% from June after falling each month in 2Q. The Y853 billion ($7.9 billion) in July was the 4th largest of the past year.(kosaku.narioka@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0130 GMT - Hong Leong Investment Bank turns positive on the Malaysian ringgit after its recent sharp rebound against the dollar. The synchronization of global growth and monetary policy will continue to exert weakness on the dollar while firmer oil prices will boost the ringgit, it says. Low foreign holdings of maturing domestic bonds will limit outflows while higher export proceeds are also ringgit positive, Hong Leong says. It projects the dollar to trade at MYR4.10-4.25 for the remainder of this year and at MYR3.90-4.10 next year. The ringgit has climbed more than 6% against the dollar so far this year. (yantoultra.ngui@wsj.com; @yantoultra)\par \par \uc2 0128 GMT - China guides the yuan stronger against the dollar for the 11th session in a row. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sets the dollar's midpoint for daily trading at CNY 6.4997, compared with CNY 6.5032 on Friday. Authorities are now confronted with a surging yuan after months of working to curb investors' expectations that it would depreciate. Officials already appear to be working to slow the yuan's advance. Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing of the yuan boosted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by less than many analysts expected, while some capital controls are set to be phased out by the end of the month, The Wall Street Journal reported. (saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com; @saumvaish)\par \par \uc2 0122 GMT - OCBC says \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be more confident in managing market expectations regarding the yuan. That sentiment came amid reports that onshore banks as of today won't have to make a 20% deposit on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards, or bets that the yuan's value would fall. The dollar has dropped nearly 7% versus the yuan this year, 1/4 of that last week as the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's logged its biggest jump against the greenback in 12 years. OCBC says recent moves indicate that counter-cyclical factors for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair is playing a more-important role than unconventional administrative measures such as reserve costs. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0100 GMT - USD/CHF Intraday: Key resistance at 0.9490. Despite the pair posted a rebound, the upward potential is likely to be limited by the resistance at 0.9490 (the previous high). Even though a continuation of technical rebound cannot be ruled out, its extent should be limited. Therefore, as long as 0.9490 is not surpassed, a new test to 0.9430 and even to 0.9400 seems more likely to occur. Alternatively, only a break above 0.9490 would turn the outlook to positive with up targets at 0.9530 and 0.9570. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized 0investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9] (analysts@tradingcentral.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 10, 2017 23:29 ET (03:29 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170912ed9b00a00\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
