\par\par \b \uc2 Watch for Possible Yuan Correction Ahead -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2017\par 11:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0929 GMT - Investors should be aware of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yuan's continued strengthening, Citi says. "An excessively strong RMB would not be warranted by the economic fundamentals and the still unresolved structural imbalances," the bank says in a note. One-way yuan appreciation would face correction pressure, either induced by policy actions or driven by the market, Citi says. (liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0922 GMT - Sweden is "overdue some sort of signal of policy normalization" and the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  should follow the example of the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 , which on Wednesday raised rates for the second meeting in a row, says Carl Hammer, head of global macro and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at SEB. He says \uc2 Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is too focused on mirroring the accommodative policy of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which announces a decision later Thursday. Sweden's GDP rose 1.7% quarter-on-quarter in 2Q, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still keeps interest rates at -0.5%. "Are they going to hike in the late stage of the cycle?" Mr. Hammer says. The market was penciling in an 80% chance of a rate increase in April, but now there's only a 50% or 60% chance, Mr. Hammer says. EUR/SEK up 0.3% at 9.5436, up from 9.4953 before the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  announcement. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0913 GMT - The yuan has entered a "self-strengthening" cycle as more domestic investors transfer their dollar holdings into the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid the latter's recent gains, says Macquarie economist \uc2 Larry Hu\uc2 . China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose for a 7th-straight month in August, and the yuan's strength will put the PBoC under great pressure as it has to choose whether to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, he adds. Hu sees an opportunity for Beijing to loosen its capital- control efforts because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains. The yuan is at 16-month highs versus the greenback. (grace.zhu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0911 GMT - \uc2 Eurostat\uc2  raised its estimate for 2Q year-on-year eurozone growth to 2.3% from 2.2%, reflecting an upgrade to its measure of GDP in the third quarter of last year. That means the expansion in the 12 months to June was the strongest since the first quarter of 2011, and indicates that the step-up in the pace of recovery started a quarter earlier than previously thought. \uc2 Eurostat\uc2  left its QQ estimate unchanged at 0.6%, but nudged its annualized measure slightly higher, to 2.6% from 2.5%. In 2Q, growth was aided by a rebound in investment and a rise in exports, which will slightly ease worries about the impact of the euro's recent appreciation on activity. All in all, a set of figures that unambiguously argues for a reduction in \uc2 ECB\uc2  stimulus, were it not for the fact that inflation is stuck well below the target. (paul.hannon@wsj.com , Twitter: @PaulHannon29)\par \par \uc2 0858 GMT - The \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects the country's inflation to remain within the government's target range of between 2% and 4% this year, after it noted a spurt in the August data, with CPI rising 3.1% on year, accelerating from a 2.8% rise in July. The BSP, which kept benchmark interest rates steady last month, said in minutes of its last monetary board meeting that the balance of risks to inflation remains on the upside amid a firm outlook for the local economy. The comments are likely an indication that the bank is in no hurry to tighten policy and may remain on hold this year. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0849 GMT - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's potential comments on the euro's strength and its effect on growth and inflation should be the most important driver for the ECB outlook Thursday, Deutsche Bank strategists say. This is good reason for investors in government and corporate bonds to pay close attention to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments. Analysts generally expect the \uc2 ECB\uc2  to announce the tapering of its asset purchase program this year and implement it in 2018. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds EUR1.71 trillion of public sector bonds and EUR107.3 billion of corporate debt. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0848 GMT - \uc2 Sweden's Riksbank\uc2  didn't budge on Thursday despite strong growth and a pickup in inflation. The krona could be a reason for its caution. "Whenever the krona has strengthens substantially between meetings, it tends to outweigh other factors in the decision-making," says Johan Loef, an economist at Handelsbanken. That way the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  lowers "the risk of continued krona movements potentially derailing the positive but fragile inflation trend," he says. The krona has strengthened almost 3% since mid-June. It last trades at 9.5464 per euro, weakening from a level around 9.4953 per euro before the decision.(nina.adam@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0847 GMT - ANZ expects China's interest-rate profile barely move the next 2 years amid ongoing deleveraging efforts, which have become the "foremost important policy goal." The bank notes monetary-policy easing has been ruled out and macroprudential measures will play a larger role in debt control. It expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ultimately utilize the 7-day repo rate in reaching policy targets, with the rate influencing banks' rates with clients. The bank sees the 7-day repo reaching 2.65% by June 2019; it's at 2.45% now. (chester.yung@wsj.com; @chester_yung)\par \par \uc2 0844 GMT - Just as the primary market for new euro investment-grade corporate bond issues is picking up pace, the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy meeting should slow down activity Thursday, ING strategists say. It's not the best of days to sell new debt to credit investors, who will be looking for possible indications of when the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tapers its QE program. The \uc2 ECB\uc2  is currently buying EUR60 billion of assets, including corporate bonds, until December. September is a seasonally busy period in terms of corporate bond supply in Europe. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0842 GMT - The potential end of speculative-grade packaging companies' focus on deleveraging prompts \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  to suggest reducing exposure to the sector, especially as technical support could turn into a headwind. BB-rated issuers, like Ball and Crown, have benefitted from demand by investment-grade investors looking for yield in the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  QE era. And BB bonds are more exposed to losses due to rising sovereign yields compared to weaker parts of the junk bond market, analyst Christian Aust adds. \uc2 UniCredit\uc2 's coverage of the sector also includes \uc2 Owens-Illinois\uc2 , Ardagh, Bormioli Rocco and \uc2 Guala Closures\uc2 . (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0834 GMT - \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  recommends betting on steeper eurozone government bond yields, as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should do whatever it takes to keep short-end rates anchored. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should go to lengths to extend the duration of the QE program, RBC adds. Meanwhile, Eonia forwards imply no rate rises until spring 2019. Therefore, hawkish tilts should primarily push longer yields higher, but even there any upward pressure should be short-lived, according to RBC. A yield curve steepens when the gap between shorter and longer-dated yields widens. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0830 GMT - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves climbed for a 7th straight month to $3.091 trillion at the end of August, rising $10.81 billion from the end-July level, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data show. August's growth in reserves was less than July's $23.93 billion increase, and below economists' median forecast of a $19 billion increase. (liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 07, 2017 05:29 ET (09:29 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170912ed97009c5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
