\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Drops Further Against Yuan in Late-Afternoon Action -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2017\par 10:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0825 GMT - The dollar is trading near session lows against the yuan in onshore and offshore markets. The move is being driven by flows from Chinese banks, which are selling dollars and buying yuan both onshore and offshore, according to market participants. Moves like these often evoke speculation about whether \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the offshore market, the dollar is down 0.6% at CNH6.8175 after 2 big drops this afternoon. In the tightly-controlled onshore market, the dollar has fallen 0.3% to CNY6.8198. Recently, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has been fixing the yuan at a stronger level than where it has been trading onshore, perhaps in an attempt to prop up the yuan. "However, it seems like [the fixing approach] doesn't look very effective, so maybe the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  is starting to step up its actions," says Ken Cheung from Mizuho. (saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com; @saumvaish)\par \par \uc2 0810 GMT - India's goods-and-services tax goes into effect Saturday and will likely have its fair share of glitches, says \uc2 Kotak Securities\uc2 . As firms adjust to the new system, there will also be probable issues including a limited number of GST service providers and compliance-related cost increases. Kotak adds short-term GST impacts are likely to be no better than neutral, the economy stands to gain long-term as higher government revenue translates into higher growth potential. (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0805 GMT - Investors may not be as keen to buy the inflation-linked 0.125% 2026 gilt that the \uc2 U.K. Debt Management Office\uc2  is offering via auction Tuesday, as a further sale of this issue is scheduled for August, \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  says. The DMO is selling a further GBP1 billion of the inflation-linked bond Tuesday, pushing its total size to GBP10.45 billion, excluding post-auction proceeds. The next reopening is due August 8.(tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0802 GMT - \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  rates strategists maintains its recommendation to be long in 2027-dated Spanish bonds against those maturing in 2025 and 2030. SocGen's reiterates its recommendation as Spain is set to launch a new, October 2027-dated bond on Tuesday via a syndicate of banks. Spain's current 10-year, April 2027-dated benchmark outperformed the curve on Monday, which suggests to \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  rates strategists that the new benchmark had largely been priced in. (emese.bartha@wsj.com ; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0757 GMT - With an election year looming in 2018, the GOP will set aside differences to push tax-reform, repatriation and infrastructure-spending proposals through Congress, predicts \uc2 Nikko Asset Management\uc2 . As such, it sees near-term gains for both US stocks and the dollar. "Analysts have not adjusted their EPS forecasts for the expected Republican tax cuts," adds John Vail, the firm's chief strategist. The Japanese asset manager expects the S&P 500 to be at 2499 at the end of 3Q, versus Monday's finish of 2434 and December's mid-2017 forecast of 2478. Nikko, though, was wildly too bullish on its end-of-2016 dollar calls, predicting Y123 and parity versus the euro; both are some 10% stronger than those levels. The firm expects slight 2H gains for the dollar. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0752 GMT - The euro-denominated bonds of Schaeffler are suffering on the secondary market Tuesday, in line with the sliding stock price in Frankfurt, after the car parts maker issued a profit warning for 2017. Bid yields on the 3.75% 2026 callable bond of Schaeffler, issued by IHO Verwaltungs, surge to 2.66% from 2.44%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  data. Yields rise as bond prices drop. Other euro bonds of the speculative-grade firm are dropping in similar fashion. Shares in Schaeffler tumble by 12.1%.(tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0730 GMT - Spain goes ahead on Tuesday with the syndicated launch of a new 10-year government bond, for which Mizuho rates strategists expect a deal size of around EUR6 billion. That would match the transaction size of Spain's 10-year bond launch in July 2016 but it would be smaller than the EUR9 billion volume in January this year. A size of EUR6 billion "is reasonable," Mizuho says. Mizuho strategists Peter Chatwell and Antoine Bouvet see the fair value for the coming October 2027-dated bond at around 10 basis points above the current 10-year benchmark April 2027-dated bond which trades at 1.37%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2 . (emese.bartha@wsj.com ; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0712 GMT - The decision of German development bank KfW to offer a seven-year euro bond makes sense, at least from the issuer's standpoint, as similar outstanding debt still trades near its tightest levels versus bunds since November, ING says. The gap between the yields of KfW's 0% 2023 bond and the \uc2 German government\uc2 's 2% 2023 issues stands at 21 bps, down from wides of almost 43 bps in February, based on \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  data. Both KfW and the \uc2 German government\uc2  carry AAA ratings from the three major rating companies.(tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0710 GMT - Fitch boosts the credit rating of \uc2 Alpha Bank\uc2 's mortgage-backed covered bonds to B- from CCC+, which takes it up to the so-called country ceiling, the highest rating it can currently be given. The country ceiling is a rating cap which reflects the risk of capital and exchange controls by Greek authorities. Following Fitch's action, the mortgage bonds of Alpha, its peer Piraeus and the two covered bond programs of \uc2 National Bank of Greece\uc2  are all rated B-, the country ceiling. At least Fitch stands ready to lift the rating on all Greek banks' covered bond programs when the country ceiling rises. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0703 GMT - The dollar's sudden drop against the yuan an hour ago is attracting attention. Sue Trinh, head of Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at RBC, says some local banks sold greenbacks and bought yuan onshore this afternoon, though she's not sure whether the move was the result of \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar dropped as much as 0.4% against the yuan onshore, but it's rebounded some to sit 0.2% lower on the session at CNY6.8269, according to Wind Info. Meanwhile, offshore trading "took a cue" from the onshore action, according to Trinh. The dollar is down 0.4% at CNH6.8272. (saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com; @saumvaish)\par \par \uc2 0650 GMT - Yields on the German 2-year benchmark bond, or schatz, have been rising steadily in recent weeks and seem unlikely to return to all-time lows set earlier this year, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  strategist Rainer Guntermann says in a note. Debt supply gives investors "abundant collateral," while general collateral rates - the rates applying on borrowing against the range of assets accepted in repos - are feeling upward pressure from the U.S, he adds. The 0.5% 2019 German bond is trading at yields of minus 0.63% Tuesday, up from minus 0.96% in February, based on \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  data. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0645 GMT - As the BoJ continues to keep interest rates pinned at ultralow levels, Japanese households have started to seek higher yields in government bonds. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data show the share of JGBs held by households rose 1.2% from a year earlier in 1Q, the first increase since 4Q08 at the height of the global financial crisis. Likely helping demand to start 2017 was minimum payouts guaranteed on JGBs for individual investors, says Tsuyoshi Ueno, senior economist at the NLI Research Institute. (megumi.fujikawa@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 27, 2017 04:25 ET (08:25 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170627ed6r000lc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
