\par\par \b \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s Yuan Makes Biggest Leap in Five Months\b0\par\par\uc2 784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2017\par 06:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  guided the yuan to its biggest one-day jump in roughly five months Thursday, the latest sign that authorities are seeking to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of the downgrade of the country\u8217\'20\'19s sovereign debt by \uc2 Moody\u8217\'20\'19s Investors Service\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 The People\u8217\'20\'19s Bank of China\uc2  set the dollar\u8217\'20\'19s daily midpoint for trading at 6.8090 yuan, meaning the yuan was at its strongest since Nov. 10. This strong \u8220\'20\'1Cfix,\u8221\'20\'1D which takes into account where the yuan finished trading the day before, came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged against the dollar in onshore trading Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The yuan rose even higher after trading began at 9:30 a.m. local time Thursday. That is a change from recent weeks, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  guided the yuan to stronger-than-expected levels, only to watch it weaken once trading began.\par \par \uc2 Shifting expectations about the yuan\u8217\'20\'19s short-term fortunes are driving the change.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tweaked the mechanism for setting the daily fix last Friday, in effect taking even more control over the value of the yuan\u8212\'20\'14which has helped persuade investors that it is committed for now to strengthening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The new method could also help smooth swings against the dollar. As a result, many analysts have revised their forecasts for the yuan, and now project a smaller decline or even a slight gain for this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  is telling investors is that the [yuan] can appreciate against the U.S. dollar,\u8221\'20\'1D said Larry Hu, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Macquarie.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the onshore market in recent days, traders say, directing state-owned banks to buy yuan and sell dollars to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Without that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have become so strong, said a Shanghai-based senior trader with a domestic bank.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe key question for everyone now is when the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  will let this round of appreciation end,\u8221\'20\'1D the trader said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are quite uncertain times for yuan traders.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Soaring borrowing costs for the yuan in Hong Kong have also propelled the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher outside of China, where it trades more freely. That overnight yuan borrowing rate hit 42.82% on Thursday, up from 21.08% on Wednesday. The offshore yuan rose as much as 0.3% from its level late Wednesday before giving up its gain; it was recently down 0.2% at 6.7591 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 There are several theories as to why Beijing is allowing the yuan to strengthen so much right now.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts and traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be pre-emptively warning investors off betting against the yuan in an effort to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable. While the \uc2 Moody\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  downgrade on May 24 didn\u8217\'20\'19t reveal any new fragilities in China\u8217\'20\'19s economy, it highlighted the risks associated with the rapid debt buildup that is fueling recent growth.\par \par \uc2 Another theory is that \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking the opportunity afforded by the dollar\u8217\'20\'19s weakness against several \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the yuan. That should provide more leeway to allow weakening against the dollar later this year if the economy cools or the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raises interest rates further.\par \par \uc2 Allowing the yuan to rise more against the dollar could also be a way to stem its fall against trading partners\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yuan had already been rising against the dollar before its recent dramatic moves, but the Korean won and Mexican peso were rising faster. An index of the yuan\u8217\'20\'19s value against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell Friday to its lowest level since it was first published by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2015.\par \par \uc2 Or it could be to help make China\u8217\'20\'19s domestic bonds more attractive to foreign investors, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has approved a bond-connect program between the mainland and Hong Kong. China has been trying to attract foreign money into its domestic markets; net capital outflows rose to more than $20 billion in April, according to the Institute of International Finance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody wants to invest in a country when you expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mirza Baig, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest-rate strategy for Asia at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Correction \uc2 The People\u8217\'20\'19s Bank of China\uc2  may be propping up the yuan to deter investors from betting against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts say. An earlier version of this article incorrectly said it was to deter bets against the yen. (June 1, 2017)\par \par \uc2 Write to Saumya Vaishampayan at saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 01, 2017 00:10 ET (04:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170601ed610008z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
