\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2017\par 15:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Oil Prices Fall After \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Extends Output Cut \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude prices fell after major oil producers extended output cuts by less than some investors had hoped. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. Stock Futures Point Higher Despite Pressure on Energy Shares \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks were poised to extend gains even as a fall in oil prices weighed on energy companies. Futures pointed to a 0.3% opening advance for the S&P 500. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. Jobless Claims Rose Slightly Last Week \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 he number of Americans applying for first-time unemployment benefits ticked up last week, though overall numbers remain consistent with steady job gains. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ's Daily Shot: Amount of Time Homes Sit on the Market Reaches a New Low \par  \par  \par China Hitches Yuan to the Dollar, Buying Rare Calm \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears to have effectively pegged the Chinese yuan to the dollar in recent weeks, a policy twist that has helped stabilize the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a year of political transition. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Agrees to Extend Crude Output Caps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  renewed an agreement to withhold some crude-oil supplies into March 2018, doubling down on its bet that it can raise prices despite soaring output from U.S. shale producers. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK Growth Slower Than First Thought in 1Q \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. economy slowed more sharply than first thought in the first quarter, a warning sign on growth ahead of a national election June 8 and the start of Brexit talks with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BIS Releases New Set of Standards for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Trading \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A group of global standards-setters on Thursday completed a new set of principles for trading in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, capping a two-year effort to improve transparency after a series of collusion scandals at major banks. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Where the China Credit Crunch Could Really Bite \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  didn't say this week is that China's sovereign bailout of troubled state companies is in fact already well under way, with a little help from provincial governments. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Beijing on the China-U.S. Trade Relationship: It's All Good \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's assessment of the trade relationship with the U.S.: The imbalance isn't that bad, job losses at U.S. steel mills aren't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fault and Beijing's yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  benefit the U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 25, 2017 09:00 ET (13:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170525ed5p001m7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
