\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2017\par 13:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Crude Prices Drop Ahead of OPEC Deal on Output Cuts \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude prices fell after a Saudi oil minister suggested that output cuts won't be extended by more than nine months in a meeting of oil major producers. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Agrees to Extend Crude Output Caps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  renewed an agreement to withhold some crude-oil supplies into March 2018, doubling down on its bet that it can raise prices despite soaring output from U.S. shale producers. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Europe Shares Reverse Gains on OPEC News \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European stocks reversed early gains as an update from major energy producers around an \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  meeting prompted steep swings in oil prices. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BIS Releases New Set of Standards for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Trading \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A group of global standards-setters on Thursday completed a new set of principles for trading in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, capping a two-year effort to improve transparency after a series of collusion scandals at major banks. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Where the China Credit Crunch Could Really Bite \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  didn't say this week is that China's sovereign bailout of troubled state companies is in fact already well under way, with a little help from provincial governments. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Beijing on the China-U.S. Trade Relationship: It's All Good \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's assessment of the trade relationship with the U.S.: The imbalance isn't that bad, job losses at U.S. steel mills aren't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fault and Beijing's yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  benefit the U.S. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Fed Should Be Judged On How Well It Achieves Mandates, Fed's Evans Says \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chicago Fed Chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Charles Evans\f28 \uc2 \f2  said a conservative disposition among policy makers can make it hard to truly achieve a 'symmetric' inflation target, where price pressures above and below the target are equally unwelcome. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. Dollar Finds Unusual Favor in Hong Kong \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar has been on something of a tear-against one \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  where it ought to be quite stable. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ to Continue Monetary Easing, Says Board Member Sakurai \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  board member Makoto Sakurai said Thursday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will carry on with its easing program by keeping interest rates low and expanding its monetary base, dismissing speculation of tightening soon. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China Securities Regulator Punishes Three Domestic Brokerages \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's securities regulator punished three domestic brokerages for violating rules on margin trading with transactions on behalf of Chicago-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citadel LLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 25, 2017 07:00 ET (11:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170525ed5p0015r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
