\par\par \b \uc2 Trump 'absolutely not' trying to talk down dollar: Mnuchin\b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2017\par 11:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Reuters) - U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is "absolutely not" trying to talk down the strength of the dollar, Treasury Secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  was quoted as saying in the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Trump said last week in an interview with the Wall Street Journal that the dollar was "getting too strong", and backed away from labeling China a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator.\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin had played down that comment on the dollar in an interview first published late on Monday in the FT. In a more detailed version published on Wednesday, he directly rejected the idea that Trump was trying to talk down the dollar, saying "Absolutely not, absolutely not."\par \par \uc2 The dollar gained after Mnuchin's initial remarks late on Monday.\par \par \uc2 But on Wednesday the euro hit a three-week high as the dollar was weakened by doubts over a fiscal boost promised by the president and by the pricing out of bets on three \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  interest rates hikes this year.\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin also said the Trump administration did not deem foreign countries to be manipulating their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they did so in a way that benefited Washington.\par \par \uc2 "To manipulate a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  you have to be doing it to disadvantage the United States," he said.\par \par \uc2 Trump campaigned on a promise to label China a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator - something that could pave the way for higher U.S. tariffs - but his administration decided not to do so in a report published on April 13.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury report recognized what many analysts have said over the past year, namely that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prop up the value of the yuan, not push it lower to make Chinese exports cheaper.\par \par \uc2 Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs meet in Washington this week for the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 's twice-yearly meetings. Mnuchin said addressing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings was "one of the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's most important roles".\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by David Milliken; Editing by Louise Ireland and John Stonestreet) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-4-19T09:28:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170419ed4j00avp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
