\par\par \b \uc2 The Morning Ledger: Foreign Investors Spurn China's Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rheaa Rao \par \uc2 2,028 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2017\par 13:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Good morning. China is opening its financial markets more than ever to global investors, hoping the charm offensive will attract more money in a time of heavy capital outflows. But the anticipated flood of funds hasn't materialized, Shen Hong, Anjie Zheng and Rachel Rosenthal write.\par \par \uc2 In just over 12 months, China opened its $9 trillion bond market to overseas investors and launched a trading link between the Shenzhen and Hong Kong stock markets that gives foreigners access to shares of some of the fastest-growing companies in the Middle Kingdom. This week, Chinese investors allowed overseas investors in its bond market to buy products that enable them to hedge \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks. Nevertheless, foreign investors have been cautious.\par \par \uc2 Overseas investors' Chinese bond holdings dropped to 1.3% of the total outstanding by the end of last year, a fall from 1.4% before the market's broad opening in February 2016. Money flowing into Shenzhen stocks from Hong Kong has been tepid, averaging just 5% of the daily 13 billion yuan ($1.89 billion) quota allowed in February. The trend is similar for a trading link between Shanghai and Hong Kong set up in 2014.\par \par \uc2 Investors cite several worries, including time-consuming registration processes and confusion over the tax rules on capital gains. Some said markets in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  are too expensive. Others refer to regular state \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets, such as the heavy share buying by government-backed funds whenever Chinese stocks dip. Another worry: whether, given China's tight capital controls, investors will be able to get their money out of China as readily as it is being welcomed in.\par \par \uc2 THE DAY AHEAD\par \par \uc2 Markets to digest Yellen speech. Federal Reserve Chairwoman \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  is scheduled to speak on the economic outlook at 1 p.m., one day before the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  goes quiet in the run-up to its March 14-15 policy meeting, \uc2 Marketwatch\uc2  reports. Ms. Yellen's speech comes after Fed governor \uc2 Lael Brainard\uc2  earlier this week said another rate rise would be "appropriate soon."\par \par \uc2 CORPORATE NEWS\par \par \uc2 Snap Inc\uc2 . trade surges 44% in market debut. The company's shares opened at $24, above its initial public offering of $17. The Wall Street Journal's reporters followed Snap's first day as a publicly traded company.\par \par \uc2 Bet on \uc2 Snap Inc\uc2 . shows the role of luck in venture business. \uc2 Lightspeed Venture Partners\uc2 ' $8 million investment has now yielded stock that could be worth around $1.5 billion. This estimate was while \uc2 Snap Inc\uc2 . priced its IPO at $17 a share, it is now worth $24 a share.\par \par \uc2 More than 1,800 \uc2 Boeing Co\uc2 . employees accept voluntary buyouts. The move comes at a time the aerospace company seeks to slash costs, boost efficiency and profit margins.\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs Group Inc\uc2 .'s new rules on mobile perks leaves employees grumbling. The firm's new data and voice reimbursement policy went into effect on Wednesday, Bloomberg reports. This is part of the firm's efforts to cut costs.\par \par \uc2 Procter & Gamble Co\uc2 . doubles down on demands of digital ad giants. The biggest advertising spender in the world is ramping up the pressure on the internet's most dominant marketing platforms to urgently implement safeguards and independent verification to assure advertisers that their money is well spent.\par \par \uc2 Toshiba\uc2  mulls unit sale . \uc2 Toshiba Corp\uc2 . is preparing a potential $2 billion divestment of smart-meter group \uc2 Landis+Gyr\uc2 , hoping to rake in capital after a major write-down on its U.S. nuclear unit last month, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Saudi Aramco\uc2  cuts prices. \uc2 Saudi Arabian Oil Co\uc2 . has lowered prices for almost all of its crude grades for April delivery. The world's largest oil exporter, known as \uc2 Saudi Aramco\uc2 , said on Thursday that it had reduced superlight and extra-light crude prices for its customers in the Far East, its largest market, by 50 cents and 75 cents, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Shipbuilder seizes Trump challenge to deliver on price. Chief Executive Mike Petters, the head of the Navy's largest shipbuilder, \uc2 Huntington Ingalls Industries Inc\uc2 ., said the president's approach is a chance to build more ships and boost ongoing cost-cutting efforts, instead of a challenge to profits.\par \par \uc2 Sky\uc2  bid will boost British TV, says Murdoch. A proposed GBP11.7 billion ($14.3 billion) takeover of the British broadcaster \uc2 Sky PLC\uc2  by America's \uc2 21st Century Fox Inc\uc2 . will ensure that the U.K.'s creative industry can compete better overseas and secure hundreds of millions of pounds of annual investment, \uc2 James Murdoch\uc2  said, as reported by the Times. \uc2 21st Century Fox\uc2  and Wall Street Journal-owner News Corp share common ownership.\par \par \uc2 Glencore\uc2  paid Gertler in Congo deals. \uc2 Glencore PLC\uc2  paid at least $100 million to controversial Israeli billionaire Dan Gertler over the course of four years, in the latest revelations surrounding the miner's activities in the Congo, the Telegraph reports.\par \par \uc2 Bridgewater Associates LP\uc2 's founder to step down. \uc2 Ray Dalio\uc2  will step down as co-chief executive of the hedge fund. This marks the fifth chief executive at Bridgewater since the beginning of 2016.\par \par \uc2 Bankia sees high demand for bond sale. \uc2 Bankia SA\uc2 , the Spanish bank bailed out in 2012, attracted EUR4.8 billion (5.04 billion) in demand for subordinated bonds worth EUR500 million, the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  reports. The bank is still majority owned by the government.\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  backed firm weighs potential sale. Perseus Inc., a telecommunication services provider backed by \uc2 Goldman Sachs Group Inc\uc2 ., is considering a sale. The company could be valued at $80 million to $120 million.\par \par \uc2 Arconic Inc\uc2 . appoints new board member. The company appointed \uc2 David Hess\uc2 , a former aerospace executive, effective March 10. The move comes amid pressure from activist investor \uc2 Elliott Management Corp\uc2 . to overhaul its board.\par \par \uc2 Brigham Resources LLC closes asset sale to \uc2 Diamondback Energy Inc\uc2 . The oil and gas company sold all of its West Texas assets for $2.55 billion. This was nearly four years after it received a $650 million equity investment from three private-equity firms.\par \par \uc2 REGULATION\par \par \uc2 Federal agents search \uc2 Caterpillar Inc\uc2 . locations. Federal agents searched three \uc2 Caterpillar\uc2  facilities near the Illinois headquarters of the company, which has disclosed receiving federal subpoenas seeking information related to movements of cash between the company's U.S. and foreign subsidiaries. Chief Executive Jim Umpleby apologized to the firm's employees and pledged to continue cooperating with federal authorities.\par \par \uc2 SEC's Piwowar criticizes Obama-era retirement-savings rule. The acting head of the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  blasted a regulation opposed by stockbrokers and the Trump administration, saying the rule was written to "increase profits" for trial lawyers.\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 's revised capital plan approved. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  received approval from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  for a revised plan to return capital to shareholders, a positive development for the bank after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebuked its planning processes in last year's "stress tests."\par \par \uc2 CFPB puts credit-reporting firms on notice. The head of the \uc2 Consumer Financial Protection Bureau\uc2  on Thursday urged credit-reporting companies to improve how they resolve disputes with consumers and vowed to keep scrutinizing the accuracy and quality of credit reports.\par \par \uc2 EARNINGS\par \par \uc2 Higher costs take a toll on \uc2 Costco Wholesale Corp\uc2 .'s profit. \uc2 Costco\uc2  has decided to raise membership fees for the first time since 2011. Fees are its main profit driver and the need for an increase came after a holiday quarter in which high costs offset strong sales.\par \par \uc2 Abercrombie & Fitch Co\uc2 . fails to end sales slump. The retailer's marketing shift in order to revamp its brand didn't show any signs of luring shoppers. It reported its fourth consecutive quarter of declining same-store sales.\par \par \uc2 WPP\uc2  hit by slow growth . Shares in \uc2 WPP PLC\uc2  fell more than 6% after the world's largest advertising company reported its slowest quarter of revenue growth since 2012 and sounded a cautious tone about 2017.\par \par \uc2 A case for Hollister's spin off. \uc2 Abercrombie & Fitch Co\uc2 .'s trendy Hollister brand stood out in its parent company's earnings, Bloomberg Gadfly reports. It posted its second consecutive quarter of year-over-year sales growth. Hollister might be able to put up a better fight against competitors without a parent company to weigh it down.\par \par \uc2 London Stock Exchange\uc2  raises dividend. The \uc2 London Stock Exchange Group PLC\uc2  will offer shareholders a 20% increase in their full-year dividend, following a 17% rise in total income in 2016 to GBP1.7 billion. Operating profit rose 6% to GBP426.1 million, the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 Barnes & Noble Inc\uc2 . sales continue to drop. Sales fell to $1.3 billion, down 8% from the same period a year ago. It posted a disappointing holiday quarter and gave a downbeat forecast for the fiscal year that ends in April.\par \par \uc2 Burlington Stores Inc\uc2 . profit climbs. Its profit rose 27% last quarter as comparable-store sales increased 4.6%. The results come amid declining sales of other brick-and-mortar retailers.\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 U.S. jobless claims lowest since 1973. The number of Americans applying for unemployment fell by 19,000 to a seasonally adjusted 223,000 last week. This is its lowest level in 44 years.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats concerned about jobs data under President Trump. Prominent Senate Democrats are raising concerns about the independence and integrity of the Labor Department's statistical bureau under President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's administration.\par \par \uc2 Inflation returns to Japan. Japan's consumer prices rose for the first time in more than a year in January as higher oil prices world-wide gave Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  and the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  a helping hand in their campaign to overcome deflation.\par \par \uc2 Nigeria fights to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In a two-year battle to defend the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Africa's largest oil producer is resorting to a new weapon: armed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  police.\par \par \uc2 CFO MOVES\par \par \uc2 3 Mar 2017 07:56 ET  The Morning Ledger: Foreign Investors Spurn -2-\par \par \uc2 Cesca Therapeutics Inc\uc2 ., a Rancho Cordova, Calif., therapeutics-research firm, announced mutual termination of CFO \uc2 Michael Bruch\uc2 's employment, effective March 10. Mr. Bruch will be replaced by Jeff Cauble. Mr. Cauble has been with the company since 2010 and has served as accounting manager, assistant controller and director of finance. There will be no immediate changes to his compensation.\par \par \uc2 Knightswood Financial Corp\uc2 ., a Vancouver, British Columbia, merchant-banking services firm, announced the resignation of its finance chief, Amelia Yeo, effective immediately. Ms. Yao has been with company for seven years.\par \par \uc2 THE WEEKEND READER\par \par \uc2 Every weekend we select a handful of in-depth articles we think are worth a bit of your time, either because they peel back the layers on a compelling business story, or somehow make us look at business in a different light.\par \par \uc2 Betting on the American dream. This New Yorker article explores how activist investor \uc2 Bill Ackman\uc2  and former journalist Christine Richard relied on each other to determine what was going on in companies like \uc2 MBIA Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 Herbalife Ltd\uc2 . Sheelah Kolhatkar highlights the dissent the two faced, particularly as they railed against \uc2 Herbalife\uc2 , a company that a lot of people believed helped them be more financially secure.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  may not be killing retail jobs. Research on \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 .'s large-scale eradication of jobs has confused correlation for causation, Geoffrey A. Manne and Jennifer Maclean write for Wired. The article acknowledges that the e-commerce giant is grabbing a larger share of retail sales, but proffers that its rise could mean more jobs in related fields such as manufacturing, transportation and logistics.\par \par \uc2 Family-controlled conglomerates are hurting South Korean businesses. Chaebols have seen many attempts to reform fail and have survived many crises, Bruce Einhorn, Sohee Kim and Jungah Lee write for Bloomberg Businessweek. The chaebol system refers to family-controlled conglomerates that have long dominated South Korea. The state has mounted pressure on chaebols again, after the arrest of \uc2 Samsung Electronics Co\uc2 .'s heir apparent Jay Y. Lee.\par \par \uc2 The Morning Ledger from CFO Journal cues up the most important news in corporate finance every weekday morning. Send us tips, suggestions and complaints: kimberly.johnson@wsj.com. \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 03, 2017 07:56 ET (12:56 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170303ed33001b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
