\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS-Surging dollar skittles euro, yen and EM  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 815 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2016\par 11:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Dollar index near 14-year high after upbeat US data               \par \par \uc2 * Yen, euro, emerging market cen banks seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Yuan near 7 per dollar level for first time since May 2008               \par \par \uc2 * India's rupee, Turkish lira at record low               \par \par \uc2 * Prospects of China, U.S. inflation buoy copper, zinc               \par \par \uc2 * Crude oil little changed amid \uc2 OPEC\uc2  meeting uncertainty               \par \par \uc2 By Marc Jones               \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Nov 24 (Reuters) - The dollar surged to a near 14-year high on Thursday, clocking up a string of milestones against other top world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and clobbering emerging markets.               \par \par \uc2 Stronger data from the world's biggest economy underpinned the greenback's gains, which were further amplified by thinner volumes as U.S. traders stayed away for the Thanksgiving holiday.               \par \par \uc2 The dollar pushed its way past more of last year's peaks against the euro to hit $1.0550 in early European action, with only the March 2015 high of $1.0457 standing in the way of a drive towards parity.               \par \par \uc2 The yen skidded to an eight-month low and China's yuan to an 8-1/2 year low, while the highly sensitive Turkish lira and Indian rupee hit new historic troughs.               \par \par \uc2 "There doesn't seem to be anything stopping U.S. yields going higher in the near-term so I think people are going to stay on the dollar trend," said Michael Metcalfe, head of global macro strategy at \uc2 State Street Global Markets\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 "The only risk to this are that the dislocations in markets outside of the U.S., particularly in emerging markets, get to a point where they start to feed back into concerns (for the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  as it looks to raise interest rates)," he said.               \par \par \uc2 In contrast to all the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  noise, European shares  saw a broadly quiet start, with most of the main bourses  edging marginally higher on gains from chemical and insurance firms.               \par \par \uc2 German business confidence data showed firms remained unfazed, for now at least, by the U.S. election win for Donald Trump and the political uncertainty currently bubbling in euro zone peers such as Italy.               \par \par \uc2 However, the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  delivered an unusually downbeat message, warning that global political shifts could compound existing vulnerabilities to rising interest rates and revive worries about the euro zone's weaker sovereigns.               \par \par \uc2 "This in turn could delay much-needed fiscal and structural reforms and could in a worst-case scenario reignite pressures on more vulnerable sovereigns," it added. "In particular, concerns about debt sustainability might re-emerge despite relatively benign financial market conditions."               \par \par \uc2 EMERGING STRAINS               \par \par \uc2 It was enough to keep bond markets playing the transatlantic divide that has been widening again on bets that, while the United States may be about to raise interest rates, Europe is unlikely to follow suit for a couple of years.               \par \par \uc2 The yield on Germany's 10-year government bond, the benchmark for the region, fell 4.2 basis points to 0.24 percent, while Italy, which has been plagued by political concerns ahead of a referendum on constitutional reform, outperformed with yields down 7 basis points to 2.06 percent.               \par \par \uc2 In the United States on Wednesday, the two-year government bond yield hit its highest since April 2010.               \par \par \uc2 The firm dollar kept most emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ropes, with China's yuan nearing the 7 per dollar level for the first time since May 2008.               \par \par \uc2 State banks or \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , India, Indonesia and the Philippines were all suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the slide in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said. Turkey's lira and India's rupee both rang in record lows.               \par \par \uc2 MSCI's broadest index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan  lost 0.4 percent, though the drop in the yen lifted the export-orientated Nikkei in Tokyo to a near 11-month high.               \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's Hang Seng shed 0.2 percent while higher metals prices lifted China's blue-chip CSI300 index  0.4 percent.               \par \par \uc2 Oil prices were little changed amid all the dollar commotion and ahead of a planned \uc2 OPEC\uc2 -led cut in crude production at a meeting on Nov. 30.               \par \par \uc2 U.S. crude was up 3 cents at $47.99 a barrel and Brent was flat at $48.95.               \par \par \uc2 Industrial metals remained red-hot on hopes of a revival in U.S. manufacturing and infrastructure spending under Trump. London zinc hit an 8-year high and copper jumped for a fourth day in a row to put $6,000 a tonne within reach.               \par \par \uc2 "Strong durable goods orders in the U.S. helped buoy investors who have viewed Trump's upcoming presidency as a positive for industrial metals demand," said ANZ in a report.                              \par \par \uc2 For Reuters new Live Markets blog on European and UK stock markets see reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url={\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://emea1.apps.cp.extranet.thomsonreuters.biz/cms/?pageId=livemarkets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://emea1.apps.cp.extranet.thomsonreuters.biz/cms/?pageId=livemarkets}}}\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-11-24T11:25:44.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020161124ecbo00gto\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
