\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Yuan falls to 8-year low as China-critic Trump prepares to take office\b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2016\par 08:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds comments)\par     By Michelle Chen\par     HONG KONG, Nov 16 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened to an\par eight-year low on Wednesday as expectations of higher U.S.\par interest rates buoyed the dollar, putting Beijing's commitment\par to market-oriented reforms in the spotlight as fierce critic\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  prepares to take office.\par     The yuan has now depreciated 5.4 percent against the dollar\par so far this year, with its descent gathering speed since Trump's\par election in the presidential race on Nov. 8, which has boosted\par the greenback against most other global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Trump has threatened to label China a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulator\par on his first day in office and has threatened to slap punitive\par tariffs on Chinese imports. \par     Prior to the market open, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set a\par weaker midpoint for the ninth consecutive day as the dollar\par stood near an 11-month high against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint at 6.8592 per dollar,\par weaker than the previous fix of 6.8495. \par     In the spot market, the yuan opened at 6.8608 per\par dollar and was changing hands at 6.8700 at midday, 135 pips away\par from the previous late session close and 0.16 percent away from\par the midpoint. \par     "We are still waiting for clearer signs of whether the\par dollar index can stand still above 100 and whether \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will take action to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market," said\par a trader at a Chinese bank in Shanghai.\par     "Our strategy now is to keep our positions low to minimize\par risk," the trader said.\par     The Thomson Reuters/HKEX Global CNH index, which\par tracks the offshore yuan against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a\par daily basis, stood at 94.89, weaker than the previous day's\par 95.01. \par     The global dollar index fell to 100.08 from the\par previous close of 100.23. \par     The offshore yuan was trading 0.16 percent weaker than the\par onshore spot at 6.8807 per dollar. \par     "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's authorities may have scaled back \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  given\par the broad-based nature of the dollar gains, a desire to conserve\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves and a new focus on effective exchange rate stability\par (against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rather than against the\par dollar)," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard Chartered\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said in a report on\par Wednesday.\par     A more substantial effort to contain yuan volatility may\par only emerge if spot approaches 7 per dollar before year-end, the\par bank said.\par     Stanchart said it has lowered its forecast for the yuan to\par 6.9 by end-2016 and 7.06 by end-2017, from 6.75 and 6.78,\par respectively.\par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts\par (NDFs), considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 7.0615, 2.86 percent away from the midpoint.\par     One-year NDFs are settled against the midpoint, not the spot\par rate.\par \par     The yuan market at 0729 GMT: \par     \par     ONSHORE SPOT:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.8592   6.8495    -0.14%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.87     6.8565    -0.20%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.16%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -5.48%\par  Spot change since 2005                20.47%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par     Key indexes:\par      \par  Item            Current     Previous  Change\par                                        \par  Thomson         94.89       95.01     -0.1\par  Reuters/HKEX                          \par  CNH index                             \par  Dollar index    100.08      100.23    -0.2\par  \par     \par     \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.8807    -0.16%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              7.0615    -2.86%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par \par     \par  (Reporting by Michelle Chen; Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-11-16T08:59:50.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020161116ecbg00cor\par }\page 