\par\par \b \uc2 China's money rates rise for 2nd week, treasury yields up amid inflation worries\b0\par\par\uc2 787 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2016\par 07:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 11 (Reuters) - China's primary money rates are set to rise for the second\par straight week, while long-term treasury yields climbed to seven-week highs as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par U.S. election win opened the door to higher inflation and exerted fresh pressure on \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to tighten liquidity to slow the yuan's depreciation.\par     The volume-weighted average rate of the benchmark seven-day repo traded in the\par interbank market, considered the best indicator of general liquidity in China, stood at 2.4160\par by midday on Friday, 11.79 basis points higher from the previous week's closing average rate.\par     Persistent signs of tighter liquidity were underscored as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC)\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 drained a net 300 billion yuan ($44.05 billion) through open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the week, the\par second consecutive weekly drain, and the biggest in a month.\par     Benchmark 10-year treasury yields are set to rise for the fifth straight day,\par spiking to 2.821 percent on Friday, the highest level since mid-September, prodding some\par analysts to call an end to the bull run in the bond market. Bond prices move inversely to\par yields.\par     "The bull market for bonds is over," said Xia Haojie, bond futures analyst at Guosen\par Futures.\par     "It's obvious that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  intends to engineer a rise in short-term rates, and\par maintain low long-term borrowing costs. But the treasury market will be under increasing selling\par pressure due to inflation risks ahead."\par     Globally, bond traders are bracing for higher inflation after Republican Trump's shock \par victory in Tuesday's presidential election, betting his plans for fiscal expansion and\par infrastructure investment will push up commodity and other prices. \par     Benchmark 10-year treasury yields jumped to the highest level in 10 months.\par     Higher global commodity prices are already reflected in China, where an index tracking\par non-ferrous metals in Shanghai rose to its highest level in more than two years. \par     Moreover, some analysts say Trump's protectionist stance on trade and his campaign pledge to\par call \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulator" would restrict \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's ability to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market.\par     "Yuan will be under greater depreciation pressure... and \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has to tighten monetary\par policies to help stabilize the yuan," said Guosen's Xia. \par     China is already grappling with signs of higher inflation. \par     Inflation data released earlier this week showed China's October consumer inflation rate\par rose to 2.1 percent from a year earlier, while producer prices rose a better-than-expected 1.2\par percent, the highest since December 2011.  \par     In its quarterly report published on Tuesday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it will maintain a prudent monetary\par policy, and take steps to prevent asset bubbles in an increasingly leveraged economy.\par   \par      The Shanghai Interbank Offered Rate (SHIBOR) for same tenor rose to 2.4020 percent, up 0.90\par basis points from the previous close. \par     The one-day or overnight rate stood at 2.2198 percent and the 14-day repo stood at 2.5603\par percent. \par     The spread of the five-year credit default swap rate on Chinese sovereign debt\par  fell 2.2 percent at 108.31.     \par   \par \par \par  Key money rates at a glance:\par   \par                   Volume-wei  Previous    Change (bps)               Volume\par                   ghted       day (%)                                \par                   average                                            \par                   rate (%)                                           \par  Interbank repo market\par  Overnight        2.2198      2.2403      -2.05                      \par                                                                      \par                                                                      \par  Seven-day        2.4201      2.4225      -0.24                      \par                                                                      \par                                                                      \par  14-day           2.5603      2.5542      +0.61                      \par                                                                      \par                                                                      \par  Shanghai stock exchange repo market\par  Overnight        2.3900      1.9400      +45.00                     380,254.7\par                                                                      0\par                                                                      \par  Seven-day<CN7DR  2.5500      2.2000      +35.00                     45,359.90\par  PO=SS>                                                              \par  14-day           2.6050      2.5850      +2.00                      2,851.20\par                                                                      \par                                                                      \par  PBOC Guidance Rates\par  Overnight        2.2300      2.2500      -2.00                      \par